# Documentation maintenance

- Docs must reflect actual implemented behavior, not planned future work
- Keep updates lightweight; `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/flows/`, `docs/entities-enums.md`, and `docs/external-services.md` are part of the installed AI-fication baseline and now exist — keep them current whenever the module map, enums, API contracts, or upstream/downstream relationships change. Do not expand them beyond what real implementation supports.
- Do not add New Relic/metrics docs or heavy Mermaid diagrams beyond the required component/sequence diagrams — this stays a lightweight POC.
- Update docs when behavior changes; skip doc updates for refactors that do not change behavior
- Specs under `specs/` describe experiments; update `tasks.md` checkboxes when tasks complete
